From 672ab3bf22f0e06b146d1ee01ac38f9e5e98d75d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: obviouslyvoid <obviouslyvoid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:51:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Flashlight file nodes, password backup partition, keep
 /vendor mounted

- flashlight: accept a direct sysfs control file in OF_FL_PATH1/2 (eg
  Samsung /sys/class/camera/flash/rear_flash), not only an LED class dir.
- OF_PASSWORD_BACKUP_PARTITION: keep the .fsec password backup on another
  partition (eg /cache) for devices without /persist, so the recovery lock
  works before data decryption. Written only after settings were read.
- OF_KEEP_VENDOR_MOUNTED (or a /vendor already mounted at startup): do not
  unmount /vendor during fstab processing when vendor services run from it,
  avoiding "Failed to unmount '/vendor' (Device or resource busy)".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 data.cpp             | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 gui/action.cpp       | 25 +++++++++++++++++++------
 orangefox.mk         | 12 ++++++++++++
 partitionmanager.cpp | 20 +++++++++++++++++---
 variables.h          |  9 ++++++++-
 5 files changed, 84 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

